416 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 245 0 R
/T ("Arduino" encompasses both the hardware boards and the software development environment, with the Arduino IDE serving as a user-friendly interface for coding and uploading programs to the board. At the heart of the Arduino Uno lies the ATmega328P microcontroller, which features 16 MHz processing power, 32 KB of flash memory for code storage, 2 KB of SRAM for data storage, and 1 KB of EEPROM for non- volatile storage. This microcontroller forms the foundation of the Arduino Uno's extensive capabilities. The board includes 14 digital I/O pins, 6 of which support PWM functionality, and 6 analog input pins, facilitating interaction with external sensors, actuators, and displays. Additionally, the Arduino Uno features a USB interface for seamless connection to computers, enabling effortless programming and communication, as well as a reset button for quick troubleshooting and built-in LEDs for visual feedback. )
/E ("Arduino" encompasses both the hardware boards and the software development environment, with the Arduino IDE serving as a user-friendly interface for coding and uploading programs to the board. At the heart of the Arduino Uno lies the ATmega328P microcontroller, which features 16 MHz processing power, 32 KB of flash memory for code storage, 2 KB of SRAM for data storage, and 1 KB of EEPROM for non- volatile storage. This microcontroller forms the foundation of the Arduino Uno's extensive capabilities. The board includes 14 digital I/O pins, 6 of which support PWM functionality, and 6 analog input pins, facilitating interaction with external sensors, actuators, and displays. Additionally, the Arduino Uno features a USB interface for seamless connection to computers, enabling effortless programming and communication, as well as a reset button for quick troubleshooting and built-in LEDs for visual feedback. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 245 0 R
/T (One of the primary strengths of the Arduino Uno is its ease of use, making it accessible to both beginners and experienced developers. The board is supported by the Arduino Integrated Development Environment \(IDE\), a user-friendly platform where users can write, edit, and upload code to the board. The IDE supports a simplified version of C++, which lowers the barrier for those new to programming. Additionally, the open-source nature of the Arduino platform means that both the hardware schematics and software libraries are freely available, encouraging a vast community of users to share projects, code, and ideas. )
/E (One of the primary strengths of the Arduino Uno is its ease of use, making it accessible to both beginners and experienced developers. The board is supported by the Arduino Integrated Development Environment \(IDE\), a user-friendly platform where users can write, edit, and upload code to the board. The IDE supports a simplified version of C++, which lowers the barrier for those new to programming. Additionally, the open-source nature of the Arduino platform means that both the hardware schematics and software libraries are freely available, encouraging a vast community of users to share projects, code, and ideas. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
