445 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 248 0 R
/T (A significant advantage of the MQ-135 is its ability to detect a broad spectrum of common air pollutants. It is sensitive to gases such as ammonia \(NH3\), nitrogen oxides \(NOx\), alcohol, carbon monoxide \(CO\), benzene, and smoke. This wide-ranging detection makes it a valuable tool for assessing overall air quality rather than just one specific gas. However, this also highlights a key limitation: the MQ-135 is a "non-specific" sensor. It cannot tell we the exact parts-per-million \(ppm\) concentration of a single gas. Instead, it provides a single combined reading that reflects the total concentration of all the gases it can detect. While this may not be suitable for precise scientific research, for applications that require a general sense of air quality and a clear warning for high pollution, this general-purpose functionality is very effective. )
/E (A significant advantage of the MQ-135 is its ability to detect a broad spectrum of common air pollutants. It is sensitive to gases such as ammonia \(NH3\), nitrogen oxides \(NOx\), alcohol, carbon monoxide \(CO\), benzene, and smoke. This wide-ranging detection makes it a valuable tool for assessing overall air quality rather than just one specific gas. However, this also highlights a key limitation: the MQ-135 is a "non-specific" sensor. It cannot tell we the exact parts-per-million \(ppm\) concentration of a single gas. Instead, it provides a single combined reading that reflects the total concentration of all the gases it can detect. While this may not be suitable for precise scientific research, for applications that require a general sense of air quality and a clear warning for high pollution, this general-purpose functionality is very effective. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
446 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 248 0 R
/T (Furthermore, the MQ-135 has other important characteristics. It requires a warm-up period, typically a few minutes after power is applied, to reach its stable operating temperature and provide accurate readings. The sensor's performance can also be affected by environmental factors like humidity and ambient temperature, which can influence its readings. Despite these factors, its simplicity and affordability make it an ideal starting point for anyone learning about gas sensing. By connecting the sensor's analog output to a microcontroller's analog-to-digital converter, one can easily measure the relative pollution level and use this data to trigger actions, display information, or simply log environmental changes over time. Itprovides a reliable and tangible way to connect a real-world problem like air pollution to afunctional electronic circuit. )
/E (Furthermore, the MQ-135 has other important characteristics. It requires a warm-up period, typically a few minutes after power is applied, to reach its stable operating temperature and provide accurate readings. The sensor's performance can also be affected by environmental factors like humidity and ambient temperature, which can influence its readings. Despite these factors, its simplicity and affordability make it an ideal starting point for anyone learning about gas sensing. By connecting the sensor's analog output to a microcontroller's analog-to-digital converter, one can easily measure the relative pollution level and use this data to trigger actions, display information, or simply log environmental changes over time. Itprovides a reliable and tangible way to connect a real-world problem like air pollution to afunctional electronic circuit. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
