/T (Resistors are also used in pull-up or pull-down configurations to set a digital signal to a known state, preventing a microcontroller pin from receiving a messy, undefined signal. Resistors come in a few different types, each with its own purpose. Carbon film resistors are the most common and affordable type, suitable for most general projects. Metal film resistors are more precise and stable, making them ideal for circuits where accuracy is very important. For applications that require a lot of power, like in power supplies or motor controls, wire wound resistors are used because they are designed to handle and dissipate a lot of heat. Finally, variable resistors, such as potentiometers, allow we to manually adjust the resistance. This is what we find in volume knobs on speakers or dimmer switches for lights, giving we a way to control the output of a circuit. )
/E (Resistors are also used in pull-up or pull-down configurations to set a digital signal to a known state, preventing a microcontroller pin from receiving a messy, undefined signal. Resistors come in a few different types, each with its own purpose. Carbon film resistors are the most common and affordable type, suitable for most general projects. Metal film resistors are more precise and stable, making them ideal for circuits where accuracy is very important. For applications that require a lot of power, like in power supplies or motor controls, wire wound resistors are used because they are designed to handle and dissipate a lot of heat. Finally, variable resistors, such as potentiometers, allow we to manually adjust the resistance. This is what we find in volume knobs on speakers or dimmer switches for lights, giving we a way to control the output of a circuit. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
