/T (A Light Emitting Diode, or LED, is a fundamental and widely used electronic component that produces light. As its name suggests, it is a type of diode, which is a semiconductor device that allows current to flow in only one direction. This makes it an incredibly efficient light source, far more so than traditional incandescent bulbs. LEDs are found everywhere today, from indicator lights on electronic devices and modern vehicle headlights to large display screens and traffic lights. Their small size, durability, and low power consumption have made them an indispensable part of modern electronics. )
