/T (The basic operation of an LED is quite simple. When an electrical current passes through the LED in the correct direction \(from the anode, or positive leg, to the cathode, or negative leg\), the atoms within its semiconductor material release energy in the form of light. This process is known as electroluminescence. Unlike a filament bulb, which gets hot to produce light, an LED generates very little heat. This is a key reason for its high energy efficiency and exceptionally long lifespan. The color of the light an LED emits is determined by the specific materials used in the semiconductor chip, which is why we have LEDs in a full )
