610 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 260 0 R
/T (The working of air quality monitoring system is based on three stages, sensing, processing and output. This simple methodology allows for effective real-time environmental monitoring. The core of our system is the MQ-135 gas sensor , continuously sampling the surrounding air. The MQ-135 is designed to detect a wide range of harmful gases, including ammonia, nitrogen oxides, and carbon dioxide. As the concentration of these gases in the air changes, the sensor's internal resistance also changes. This change in resistance is converted into a varying electrical signal, which is then sent to the Arduino microcontroller for analysis. This analog signal provides the raw data about the air's quality at any given moment. )
/E (The working of air quality monitoring system is based on three stages, sensing, processing and output. This simple methodology allows for effective real-time environmental monitoring. The core of our system is the MQ-135 gas sensor , continuously sampling the surrounding air. The MQ-135 is designed to detect a wide range of harmful gases, including ammonia, nitrogen oxides, and carbon dioxide. As the concentration of these gases in the air changes, the sensor's internal resistance also changes. This change in resistance is converted into a varying electrical signal, which is then sent to the Arduino microcontroller for analysis. This analog signal provides the raw data about the air's quality at any given moment. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
611 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 260 0 R
/T (Serving as the central processing unit, the Arduino Uno receives the analog signal from the MQ-135 sensor through its analog input pin \(A0\). Our custom-written code, uploaded to the Arduino, translates this raw analog signal into a meaningful numerical value, typically ranging from 0 to 1023. This value directly corresponds to the concentration of pollutants in the air. The code then uses a series of conditional statements \(if-else if\) to categorize this numerical value into simple, human-readable labels such as "Excellent," "Good," "Moderate," or "Harmful!!" This classification is key to making the complex data understandable to a non-technical audience. )
/E (Serving as the central processing unit, the Arduino Uno receives the analog signal from the MQ-135 sensor through its analog input pin \(A0\). Our custom-written code, uploaded to the Arduino, translates this raw analog signal into a meaningful numerical value, typically ranging from 0 to 1023. This value directly corresponds to the concentration of pollutants in the air. The code then uses a series of conditional statements \(if-else if\) to categorize this numerical value into simple, human-readable labels such as "Excellent," "Good," "Moderate," or "Harmful!!" This classification is key to making the complex data understandable to a non-technical audience. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
612 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 260 0 R
/T (Finally, the system outputs the processed information and provides alerts. The 16x2 LCD display is used to visually present the current air quality status, showing both the corresponding text label and numerical value. This provides immediate, on-the-spot feedback to the user. Additionally, for safety, our system includes an alert mechanism. When the processed sensor value exceeds a critical threshold, our code activates both a red LED and a buzzer. The flashing light and audible alarm serve as an warning of dangerously high pollution levels, prompting community members to take immediate protective action. )
/E (Finally, the system outputs the processed information and provides alerts. The 16x2 LCD display is used to visually present the current air quality status, showing both the corresponding text label and numerical value. This provides immediate, on-the-spot feedback to the user. Additionally, for safety, our system includes an alert mechanism. When the processed sensor value exceeds a critical threshold, our code activates both a red LED and a buzzer. The flashing light and audible alarm serve as an warning of dangerously high pollution levels, prompting community members to take immediate protective action. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
