695 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 266 0 R
/T (Our project highlighted the significant social impact of providing accessible environmental data. It showed that simple, open-source technology can empower a community with the knowledge needed to make informed health decisions, particularly benefiting vulnerable populations like children and the elderly. By making the invisible threat of air pollution visible and tangible, our system fosters increased environmental awareness and facilitates collective action. Economically, the low cost of the components, including the Arduino and MQ-135 sensor, justifies its use for widespread deployment, making a high-impact solution available on a modest budget. While a challenge was the precise calibration of the sensor to specific pollutant concentrations, the system's ability to accurately track and alert based on relative changes in air quality proved to be highly valuable for local monitoring. Overall, the project validated the use of a simple, Arduino-based system as an impactful, cost-effective, and practical tool for local air quality monitoring, laying a strong foundation for future advancements and broader community adoption. )
/E (Our project highlighted the significant social impact of providing accessible environmental data. It showed that simple, open-source technology can empower a community with the knowledge needed to make informed health decisions, particularly benefiting vulnerable populations like children and the elderly. By making the invisible threat of air pollution visible and tangible, our system fosters increased environmental awareness and facilitates collective action. Economically, the low cost of the components, including the Arduino and MQ-135 sensor, justifies its use for widespread deployment, making a high-impact solution available on a modest budget. While a challenge was the precise calibration of the sensor to specific pollutant concentrations, the system's ability to accurately track and alert based on relative changes in air quality proved to be highly valuable for local monitoring. Overall, the project validated the use of a simple, Arduino-based system as an impactful, cost-effective, and practical tool for local air quality monitoring, laying a strong foundation for future advancements and broader community adoption. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
