1228 0 obj
<<
/Title (Air quality is a critical factor that affects the health of people and the planet. This project details a simple and cost-effective air quality monitoring system. The system uses MQ135 gas sensor to measure the levels of harmful substances present in the air. A Arduino UNO is used to process the data from the sensor. The processed data is then used to show the current air quality level through a LCD display. This will help increase public awareness about pollution. The system is designed to be compact and use low-cost components. This makes it suitable for many uses, including education and small-scale environmental projects. The data collected by the system can show the possible health effects of air pollution. It can also help in the development of more advanced monitoring systems. Importantly, it also helps people learn more about the environment and the importance of clean air. Air pollution is a significant environmental problem. It causes harm to human health and damages the earth's ecosystems. This system provides a practical way to track pollution levels. It can be used in schools to teach students about air quality. It can also be used in communities to help residents understand the air they breathe. A key goal is to make air quality data easily accessible to everyone. This empowers individuals to make informed choices and take action to protect themselves and their families. The system can also assist researchers in their work. Scientists can use the data to study the sources and effects of air pollution. This project demonstrates the process of building a basic air quality monitoring tool. It uses simple components and programming. It can help students and others learn about air pollution and how to measure it. The project also provides a foundation for creating more complex systems. These advanced systems can provide more detailed information. They can also be used to develop strategies toreduce and solve air pollution problems.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 788 0 R
/Next 1229 0 R
>>
endobj
