1405 0 obj
<<
/Title (A key next step is to explore how to manage and use data more effectively. Integrating a data logging system would allow the device to save air quality readings over time, like a diary. This historical data can then be processed to identify pollution patterns and trends. We can also add wireless connectivity, such as a Wi-Fi module, which would let us send this data to a cloud platform. This would allow for the collection of information from many devices and the creation of a real-time air quality map of the community. This ability to see and analyze data from anywhere would greatly enhance the system's convenience and its ability to provide community- wide insights.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 789 0 R
/Prev 1232 0 R
/Next 1406 0 R
>>
endobj
1406 0 obj
<<
/Title (Furthermore, we can enhance the system's hardware to provide a more detailed and durable solution. We plan to add more specific sensors to measure pollutants like fine dust particles \(PM2.5\) and carbon monoxide \(CO\), giving a more accurate picture of air quality. For continuous outdoor use, we will design and build a robust, waterproof enclosure to protect all the electronics. To make the device truly autonomous, we can also integrate a small solar panel and a battery, allowing it to power itself using the sun. This would make it a self-sufficient and eco-friendly device that can be placed in any location without a power outlet.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 789 0 R
/Prev 1405 0 R
/Next 1233 0 R
>>
endobj
