1693 0 obj
<<
/Title (In conclusion, the air quality monitoring system developed using an Arduino proved to be a practical and effective solution for addressing localized environmental concerns. This project successfully demonstrated the ability to provide real-time air quality data in an accessible format, a crucial need highlighted by our community survey. Our prototype reliably translated raw sensor readings from the MQ-135 into clear, understandable categories, with the LCD display confirming "Excellent" readings during testing and the buzzer/LED system providing an immediate, undeniable warning when dangerous levels were simulated.)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1549 0 R
/Next 1694 0 R
>>
endobj
1694 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project's key achievement is its ability to empower communities with direct, actionable knowledge about the air they breathe. By making an invisible threat visible, the system fosters greater environmental awareness and enables residents to make informed health decisions, particularly benefiting vulnerable populations. The low cost of the components makes this solution highly economical and justifies its widespread adoption, reinforcing its practicality as a community tool. While the initial challenge of sensor calibration required careful attention, the system's robust performance in detecting relative changes in air quality was a significant validation. Thus, this Arduino-based air quality monitoring system presents a compelling solution that combines open-source technology with a strong social purpose, laying a foundation for healthier and more informed communities.)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1549 0 R
/Prev 1693 0 R
>>
endobj
