1816 0 obj
<<
/Title (Air pollution is a critical issue with serious consequences for public health and the environment. While large cities often have effective monitoring systems, local communities frequently lack access to this vital information, leaving residents unaware of the air quality they are breathing. This problem was a key finding from a community survey we conducted in Muralinagar, Visakhapatnam, where residents expressed a strong need for an easy and affordable way to monitor their local environment. The survey revealed that residents felt a sense of powerlessness against an invisible threat and were eager for a practical tool that could provide actionable data for their daily lives, especially to protect family members. To address this pressing community need, our mini-project focuses on creating a cost-effective, easily replicable, and user-friendly air quality monitoring system. The core of our prototype is an Arduino Uno microcontroller, chosen for its open-source nature, low cost, and ease of programming. We use an MQ-135 gas sensor to detect a wide range of pollutants, providing a direct measurement of air quality. This sensor is a highly reliable and affordable option for detecting common harmful gases, making it ideal for a community-focused project. The raw data from the sensor is processed by our code, which translates complex electrical signals into easily understandable air quality metrics. This processed data is then displayed on a simple 16x2 LCD display, making the information instantly accessible and easy to read for everyone in the community, regardless of their technical background. To enhance safety and awareness, the system includes an immediate alert mechanism. When air pollution levels exceed a safe threshold, a buzzer sounds and a red LED illuminates, providing an undeniable visual and auditory warning. By developing this system with readily available components, we demonstrate how simple technology can be a powerful tool for community empowerment. This project not only serves as a functional solution but also provides a foundation for more advanced systems in the future. It is our goal to contribute to a healthier and more informed society by making environmental data accessible to all.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1806 0 R
>>
endobj
