1865 0 obj
<<
/Title (Furthermore, the MQ-135 has other important characteristics. It requires a warm-up period, typically a few minutes after power is applied, to reach its stable operating temperature and provide accurate readings. The sensor's performance can also be affected by environmental factors like humidity and ambient temperature, which can influence its readings. Despite these factors, its simplicity and affordability make it an ideal starting point for anyone learning about gas sensing. By connecting the sensor's analog output to a microcontroller's analog-to-digital converter, one can easily measure the relative pollution level and use this data to trigger actions, display information, or simply log environmental changes over time. Itprovides a reliable and tangible way to connect a real-world problem like air pollution to afunctional electronic circuit.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1858 0 R
/Prev 1875 0 R
>>
