/Title (A significant advantage of the MQ-135 is its ability to detect a broad spectrum of common air pollutants. It is sensitive to gases such as ammonia \(NH3\), nitrogen oxides \(NOx\), alcohol, carbon monoxide \(CO\), benzene, and smoke. This wide-ranging detection makes it a valuable tool for assessing overall air quality rather than just one specific gas. However, this also highlights a key limitation: the MQ-135 is a "non-specific" sensor. It cannot tell we the exact parts-per-million \(ppm\) concentration of a single gas. Instead, it provides a single combined reading that reflects the total concentration of all the gases it can detect. While this may not be suitable for precise scientific research, for applications that require a general sense of air quality and a clear warning for high pollution, this general-purpose functionality is very effective.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1858 0 R
/Prev 1886 0 R
/Next 1865 0 R
>>
endobj
