/Title (The working of air quality monitoring system is based on three stages, sensing, processing and output. This simple methodology allows for effective real-time environmental monitoring. The core of our system is the MQ-135 gas sensor , continuously sampling the surrounding air. The MQ-135 is designed to detect a wide range of harmful gases, including ammonia, nitrogen oxides, and carbon dioxide. As the concentration of these gases in the air changes, the sensor's internal resistance also changes. This change in resistance is converted into a varying electrical signal, which is then sent to the Arduino microcontroller for analysis. This analog signal provides the raw data about the air's quality at any given moment.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1867 0 R
/Next 1889 0 R
>>
endobj
1881 0 obj
<<
/Title (Finally, the system outputs the processed information and provides alerts. The 16x2 LCD display is used to visually present the current air quality status, showing both the corresponding text label and numerical value. This provides immediate, on-the-spot feedback to the user. Additionally, for safety, our system includes an alert mechanism. When the processed sensor value exceeds a critical threshold, our code activates both a red LED and a buzzer. The flashing light and audible alarm serve as an warning of dangerously high pollution levels, prompting community members to take immediate protective action.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1867 0 R
/Prev 1889 0 R
>>
endobj
