/Title (Serving as the central processing unit, the Arduino Uno receives the analog signal from the MQ-135 sensor through its analog input pin \(A0\). Our custom-written code, uploaded to the Arduino, translates this raw analog signal into a meaningful numerical value, typically ranging from 0 to 1023. This value directly corresponds to the concentration of pollutants in the air. The code then uses a series of conditional statements \(if-else if\) to categorize this numerical value into simple, human-readable labels such as "Excellent," "Good," "Moderate," or "Harmful!!" This classification is key to making the complex data understandable to a non-technical audience.)
