/Title (A buzzer is a small but powerful component used in electronics to produce sound. Its primary function is to convert an electrical signal into an audible sound, typically a "beep" or a "buzz." This makes it an essential component for adding sound-based alerts, feedback, and alarms to a wide range of projects. We can find buzzers in everything from alarm clocks and microwave ovens to fire alarms and children's toys. They provide a simple and effective way to get a user's attention without needing a complex speaker system.)
